# Security owns anything that decides who can do what.
#
# The ruleset requiring code-owner review is itself in this repo, so a PR removing it needs
# the approval of the team it protects. That circularity is intentional.

*                               @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# Merge requirements, bypass grants, push restrictions.
/modules/rulesets/              @Mindclade/security

# Actions allowlist, OIDC subject template, secrets policy.
/modules/policies/              @Mindclade/security

# Org-wide settings, App installation scope (the blast radius of a compromised App key),
# and the enterprise surface.
/modules/organization/          @Mindclade/security
/modules/enterprise/            @Mindclade/security

# The access model: teams, IdP-sourced membership, repository grants, custom properties.
/modules/teams/                 @Mindclade/security
/modules/repositories/          @Mindclade/security

# The catalogue IS the access model — a one-line YAML edit changes who can reach what.
/catalog/                       @Mindclade/security

# Composition: which modules exist and what they are wired to.
/main.tf                        @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security

# The pipeline that applies all of the above.
/.github/workflows/             @Mindclade/platform @Mindclade/security
